    "font-size": {
      "25": { "value": "0.75rem", "comment": "12px. Badge. A NEW step BELOW 50, minted 2026-08-20 when badge/font-size stopped being a percentage of its inherited context (the design system owner's de-flex ruling). NOTE the scale is abstract and gapped, NOT rem x 100 — that convention belongs to space.*. font-size.75 is already 0.9rem, so 0.75rem could not take the name its rem value suggests; it needed a step below the previous floor. 0.75rem is exactly what 75% of a 1rem context always rendered, so this value is the old body-context rendering made absolute, not a new size." },
      "50": { "value": "0.8rem", "comment": "12.8px. 4.x: $small-font-size, .is-small" },
      "75": { "value": "0.9rem", "comment": "14.4px. figcaption (90% of base). Note: $label-font-size (0.9rem) was removed from _variables.scss in 1fbefb6f94; live labels use --form-label-font-size: 1rem (form.scss)." },
